.policy "ruff-pyi046-unused-private-protocol" revision 2
.description "Use, make public or remove a private Protocol class that nothing in its file references; an unused private protocol is likely a mistake."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI046 (flake8-pyi), every file: a private Protocol class (`class _P(Protocol)`, `Protocol[T]` too) that
// nothing in the file reads. Class bodies are checked only in stubs (python/typing's unused_private). Reported
// at the class name.
//   class _P(Protocol): ...       ← PYI046 when nothing mentions _P
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI046(at: node, x: symbol) code "PYI046" "Nothing in this file uses the private protocol `{x}`. Use it, rename it without the underscore if other modules import it, or remove it once nothing does."
    suppress ruff "PYI046"
PYI046(n, x) :- unused_private(_, x, c), kind(c, "class_definition"), class_base_sym(c, q), split_dot(q, m, "Protocol"),
    typing_mod(m), field(c, "name", n).
